# ChainOpt build rules

MVP only, one flag (oversized model usage). No VS Code extension, no hosted
dashboard, no Stripe, no redundancy or parallelization flag yet. If a task
seems to call for one of those, stop and say so in your summary instead of
building it.

Always:
- Write or update a test before considering any function done.
- Run the full test suite before committing. Never commit red.
- Commit after each PLAN.md item is verified, not in larger batches.
- Cost numbers always come from real token counts and real Supabase data,
  never invented.
- End every session with a plain-English summary: what changed, what test
  proves it works, what's next in PLAN.md, anything you're unsure about.
- Stay inside the track you were asked to build. Don't touch /web without
  being asked.

Stack: Python, Supabase + pgvector, LangChain/LangGraph as the target
framework, pytest.

Structure:
/sdk — httpx patch + logging
/analyzer — CLI static analyzer
/engine — oversizing flag logic
/web — already built
/tests
PLAN.md — the checklist above, keep it updated
